/ref 17592186316385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f6dbc93-1b83-5d25-acd9-9c2c8535de5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315481} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f03cf21-0038-533a-aab9-c6147ed7f920" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "637c8c06-b50d-580c-8555-a7f2b7fa591e" :question/math-academy-id "q-342023" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=8x$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $4$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=4{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n8x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\\right).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-2,2).$ \nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}8t\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ [4{t}^{2}]_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi t}{2}\\right)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right))\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "363a3784-86cd-5624-ae01-ecfc85592e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315435} {:answer/id #uuid "e786c74c-45b3-56a6-9fc8-0de482bd1c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316399} {:answer/id #uuid "ff24cf77-0eb8-54be-85c8-fada8a265238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "363a3784-86cd-5624-ae01-ecfc85592e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315435} :answer-field/id #uuid "562b01d0-1c00-5656-95e5-e94e170b26e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b1ab9d6-d88f-54db-8898-c8776929e416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315179} {:answer/id #uuid "623cedf2-3888-5ff9-ac59-414dab43a963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi (n\\pi +5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315672} {:answer/id #uuid "7f98be46-8f13-5c49-8b77-7ff5e985b64e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25(-1)^{n}}{n{\\pi }^{2}(n\\pi +5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1ab9d6-d88f-54db-8898-c8776929e416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315179} :answer-field/id #uuid "aad26612-844b-5860-be9b-50e6ab9948ab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7431cef2-4a56-5a41-81e1-4185e67efb64" :question/math-academy-id "q-342203" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}+5y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))+{b}_{n}\\cdot n\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)) \\\\  & \\,+5(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)) \\\\  & \\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{5{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({b}_{n}n\\pi +5{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-{a}_{n}n\\pi +5{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the cosine and sine coefficients, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{a}_{0}}{2} &=0 \\\\ {b}_{n}n\\pi +5{a}_{n} &=0 \\\\ -{a}_{n}n\\pi +5{b}_{n} &=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nNext, from the second equation, \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the third equation gives\n\n$$\n-\\left(-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{5}\\right)n\\pi +5{b}_{n}=\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{5}\\cdot \\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)+\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+25)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b9914c2-c267-5af4-b108-3360dccddb44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315985} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e67bb4-c548-5d4b-b417-1b027f6f9f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316076} {:answer/id #uuid "d7906531-8bc2-5207-b0f1-73878255829f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b9914c2-c267-5af4-b108-3360dccddb44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315985} :answer-field/id #uuid "9835d1ba-3f1d-500f-a45d-e5d7f26272f5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bbae417-0ede-5df6-ba34-7ec70665057a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315281} {:answer/id #uuid "2138e5a7-2bb7-594a-9669-540e6cfe651d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315303} {:answer/id #uuid "3f34cf68-1608-5551-9f22-8a15afa40311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2138e5a7-2bb7-594a-9669-540e6cfe651d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315303} :answer-field/id #uuid "acff0cef-b324-50ce-ab92-c9101787e3c9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b798cf-8651-52ca-8d7a-1e223e97ecba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315164} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba398f4-b61e-5c5f-a290-559146657e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315987} {:answer/id #uuid "9d319715-3a18-5b03-a1e3-8f19ba2b0cb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315999} {:answer/id #uuid "dd5c5ed6-2f1c-5cc7-963a-f5413e330111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd5c5ed6-2f1c-5cc7-963a-f5413e330111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316349} :answer-field/id #uuid "be37d6d8-1eb7-53b0-a960-fe7553382b46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0f6d5f3-5213-5096-b128-e5b4d23a6bdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-342229" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)) \\\\  & \\,-(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2} &=-1 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{a}_{n} &=\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi } \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}-{b}_{n} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=2,$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, from the third equation, ${b}_{n}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}.$ Substituting this into the third equation, gives\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\right)\\frac{n\\pi }{2}-{a}_{n}=\\frac{4}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼1 & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{16}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{8}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+4)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ee7e427-46c3-5aed-9b19-381c6b43ae67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{nx}{\\pi }\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447524} {:answer/id #uuid "84d02c9f-09db-5f84-8395-ecb31c424496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447546} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cf8966-1bef-51d6-8f2d-fa9d3c63371e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{nx}{\\pi }\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447577} {:answer/id #uuid "d80d207a-d991-5083-a552-3b5c5c3785d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d80d207a-d991-5083-a552-3b5c5c3785d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447582} :answer-field/id #uuid "831873f5-dc3b-537b-bd1b-71e87ec289b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "333c0e0a-3cd4-59b2-92d6-93fd825879e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447500} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfe4bcc-fec4-5ff7-a0df-23a90cd726d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "piecewise smooth" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447554} {:answer/id #uuid "91d47c98-f7da-5274-8d04-afef06f100ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type